ina but pennsylvania will  remain tight on the republican side of  things i would say that there's only one  candidate presidential candidate that  has won pennsylvania since 1990 1988 and  that was donald trump  and he ran a race that was  different  it was wild people  following it they he created this  amazing base of support  and any republican who is not him has to  run a near perfect race mitch mcconnell  day said he believes that whoever wins  in pennsylvania that they feel very  strongly that they can win in  pennsylvania but i will tell you i think  that the republicans are just make sure  that while they have this fight and they  might have a recount john fetterman's  campaign is already off  oh fetterman he's about your size i  think right no he's shorter but yeah six  nine yeah shorter yeah yeah uh and he's  smaller he doesn't like suits he wears  sweats yeah i get i like him and in the  sense he's different but  looking at what i saw was  a fever of just battles from top like  republicans had votes going three deep  which means the numbers when you look at  who was showing up to vote the numbers  of republicans that were coming out to  vote  i don't care if you're superman running  for a democrat you should really be  afraid because  yes your campaign's getting started  early but the sheer numbers third place  is running strong which means that when  all of them come together and they have  to come together and i think they will i  think the republicans get it they're you  know  they know they've seen what's going on  they want their police forces back they  want respect back they want to get  inflation down they want to get america  back at least in the top five of  importance in this country right now so  we're seeing big numbers and i'm just  looking at how many people are showing  up at the ballot and it's a huge  difference i think the only ones who are  showing up for the democrats are the  progressives yeah because  the moderates are going you know what  we're kind of better off for the other  guys that's a good point do you think  that the republicans are going to  coalesce around mimet or mccormick or  whoever it is i do absolutely and i  think that uh  john fetterman probably doesn't want to  go up against mehmet oz because not only  is he battle tested in a really tough  primary he's got name recognition and if  you're talking about socialized medicine  who better to dissect what the  government has done to ruin health care  in this country than a doctor who has  enriched himself in the free market not  only in medicine but in entertainment as  well so he really cares about that issue  and i hope he pins jon fetterman down on  this because with inflation where it's  at and you know taxes a tax hike on the  horizon you compound that with medicare  for all we cannot afford that uh the the  healthcare industry cannot afford that  so yes i do think it's going to be very  tough i thought the madison cawhorn  thing was interesting because he had  been pulling ahead and i thought that  perhaps the former president's  endorsement of him last minute might  help but he  so far lost only by a couple percentage  points and you're absolutely right there  has to be something there it has to be  substantive there has to be policy  behind the person  we can no longer become attached to  people because of their characteristics  or their interesting life stories how  they lead and how they fleece us far  more importantly  looking at the endorsements does  donald trump still have that magic touch  oh no no doubt about it i think that uh  the fact that  from my state in ohio everybody was uh  you know looking for donald trump to  endorse them and there's a very very  potent he had a couple of misses here  there uh we discussed car thorn and some  others but i i must say a couple of  quick points number one john petterman  is enormously charismatic he does remind  me a lot of you tyrus and i i believe  that he will cross ov